35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It's a mess. People are shifting other bikes to leave, and the rain exposure makes some spots useless in winter.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The building account is nearly empty. Also, the ward park is expensive and has a long waiting list, so we can't rely on it.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,My suspicions were right. The same flats have held the best spots for years without any review. Daily riders are actually willing to pay.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Be careful. The neighbouring block tried charging money, and it led to arrears and people skipping meetings. It poisoned the atmosphere.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The paperwork is already a burden. Adding per-place billing would be a nightmare. Plus, those double-tier racks are hard to use and need maintenance.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, if the racks are too difficult, then a shared system might just increase the shoving matches I saw.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, if the daily riders are willing to pay, perhaps a managed fee is better than the current unfair stagnation.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Asuka, the fact that the same people always have the dry spots explains the resentment. We need a reset.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, a ""managed fee"" is exactly what caused the social rift next door. We should avoid creating a debtor class.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,Exactly! Who is going to chase the people who don't pay? Not me!,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we can't do racks and we can't do fees, we are left with very few logical options to ensure fairness.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,We must balance the financial need of the building with the social stability Shunichi is worried about.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,A lottery would at least break the cycle of the same households holding the best spots forever.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"A lottery is impersonal. It doesn't create the ""payer vs non-payer"" tension that a fee system does.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"As long as the lottery doesn't require a mountain of monthly paperwork, I'm open to it.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
